        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-09T21:10:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is part of a broken chain of \"helper\" methods. There should always be a single row that is \"found\" by the request, so for a setter on a single subId this should actually always be one. If it\u0027s not, then we can presume that the subId is invalid. I\u0027d like to re-do these methods so that we can pre-range-check the subId. Note that there\u0027s a bug filed to fix this.",
      "parentUuid": "42bdd724_94ddf2ac",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4562,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 4562,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "b212ad8ca71b79bb8009fce9927dd69c1b4774eb",
