    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3e5155f2_40b9ec44",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/SubscriptionController.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 4567,
      "author": {
        "id": 1609802
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-08T23:47:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know this is a TODO. It feels a bit weird now to return \"the number of records updated\" now. \n \n In above logic, if ret is not 1, it will throw IAE to caller. This means here we have only one possible value (\"1\" in normal case) to return to caller. This makes the int return value useless.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4567,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 4567,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "b212ad8ca71b79bb8009fce9927dd69c1b4774eb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ade8d731_210af9d7",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/SubscriptionController.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 4567,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-09T21:10:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not actually useless because There is a method in SubscriptionManager that\u0027s a \"helper\" for calling setters/getters in the DB, which expects a lambda with a return value of an int.\n\nI am very unhappy with this pattern, but I spoke to tgunn@, and we agreed that for now the top-level API should not return a boolean and should throw; however, all of the underneath methods translate rows-updated -\u003e boolean for return.\n\nReturning a non-integer would require duplication, and returning a meaningful integer will create confusion at this point. :-/\n\nFor comparison, see:\n\nSubscriptionManager#setOpportunistic() which uses the \"bool\"\n\nand see\n\nSubscriptionManager#setDeviceToDeviceStatusSharingContacts() which uses the proper API pattern, but just throws away the return value entirely!\n\ntl;dr, this is temporary, but I want to do code cleanups after FC.",
      "parentUuid": "3e5155f2_40b9ec44",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4567,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 4567,
        "endChar": 16
